<title>GERMANY: DEC GERMAN UNIT POSTS 96/97 LOSS.</title>
<headline>DEC GERMAN UNIT POSTS 96/97 LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Equipment Corp said on Tuesday its German subsidiary lost five million marks in 1996/97, as the unit's sales fell 13 percent to 1.5 billion marks.</p>
<p>But profit in 1997/98 was expected to reach 20 million to 25 million marks, with sales remaining at 1.5 billion, Digital Equipment GmbH finance chief Erich Baumgaertner said at a news conference.</p>
<p>For the business year that ended June 30, the parent company reported net income of $140.9 million, while divestments and currency fluctuations caused operating revenue to fall 10 percent to $13.01 billion.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
